            <ArticleTitle>[Ambulatory criteria of dry powder inhaler selection based on peak inspiratory flow recordings].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>490-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 185 patients (106 with asthma and 79 with COPD) peak inspiratory flow (PIFR) without resistance and across valves of popular in Poland dry powder inhalers (DPI): Discus, Turbuhaler and Aerolizer were recorded. &quot;In-Check&quot; device was used for these purposes. Clement-Clarke principle of minimal and optimal PIFR for lung drug deposition was accepted. According to this principle the results were presented on the attached table: [table: see text] Almost all patients with asthma and COPD can use Discus effectively, for other DPI's &quot;In Check&quot; investigation is often necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
